# Patches carry their target file's line endings inside the context lines, so
# they must be stored byte-for-byte. motor-data-producer's sources are CRLF
# upstream; normalising the patch to LF makes every context line mismatch and
# do_patch fails on a fresh clone -- while still applying fine in the working
# tree that created it, which is a nasty way to find out.
*.patch -text
